  "worked_solution": "To plot $y=-\\frac{6}{x},$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=-\\frac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934099/assets/d5d93e12275c683e0a56f0ec9a0c99540a7774879cd0f8fa69151ddba68a44fa.png)\n\n- Stretch the result by a scale factor of $6$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=-\\frac{6}{x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934099/assets/c525edcf937bfdc311acd0d7cac778802e1939dc2bd61fd3a5bf58f808712220.png)",
